    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1275">

                <pb facs="1314" n="1302" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/2–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-21T16:00:00-04:00">February 21,
                            1945—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>225. ReEmbs 240, February 20. Please inform the Prime Minister personally of the
                    Secretary General’s somewhat casual indication of <pb facs="1315" n="1303"
                        xml:id="pg1303"/> further delay. Department suggests that the Prime Minister
                    should, in Turkey’s best interest, see to it that Turkey’s signature of the
                    Mutual Aid Agreement is not delayed by the absence from Ankara of one or two
                    officials. The matter is too important to be left dangling, particularly at this
                    time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
